  "architectureInvariants": [
    "Codex and Claude use provider-specific anti-corruption adapters behind one Agent Execution port; their exit and terminal-event semantics are not interchangeable.",
    "Operation success requires a verified business/effect receipt. Process exit zero, provider subtype success, or model text alone is insufficient.",
    "Provider accounting consumes observed usage and modelUsage records. One agent turn is not assumed to equal one model request.",
    "Workspace instruction inheritance is an explicit authorized profile policy. It is never inferred from cwd or session identity; accepted instruction bytes are snapshotted and digested.",
    "A Codex launch that must suppress AGENTS.md sets project_doc_max_bytes=0; --ignore-rules only suppresses execpolicy .rules files.",
    "Provider stderr and structured output are captured as separate bounded streams because Codex JSONL did not expose the observed sandbox rejection as a structured failure event.",
    "Claude stream telemetry is allowlist-projected. Safe mode removed tools and MCP and ignored the workspace CLAUDE.md canary, but init still enumerated configured plugin, skill, and agent metadata.",
    "Provider session IDs and cwd are routing hints, not authorization. Resume is validated against tenant, RuntimeSession, workspace grant, credential generation, and custody fence before forwarding.",
    "Existing user CLI authorization may be imported only through an explicit local-authorized flow. Hosted production uses dedicated credential custody and generation CAS."
  ],
